Right, there are only sentential connectives (how else could they be truth =
functional, after all?).=C2=A0 All {A x conj y B} come from {A x B conj A y=
 B} in the same way.=C2=A0 It is an early and persistent flaw of Logjam tha=
t the local grammar of x and y is often lost in a maze of secondary matter,=
 since, ultimately, there are only terms and predicates and they are (or ou=
ght to be) obviously distinct.=C2=A0 (That they are not at the crucial poin=
t is thanks to JCB's initial decisions, one of which was to make the connec=
tions between terms primary, against the logic he was supposedly following =
-- and even against SAE, which he was actually following, usually.)=20
=20

